<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stagira</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Stageira</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stagira was an ancient Greek city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcidice">Chalcidice</a> peninsula in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, founded by settlers from Andros around 655 BCE. It is best known as the birthplace of the philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> in 384 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> destroyed it in 349 BCE, but it was later rebuilt in Aristotle's honour.</p></div>
